+# The Daily Grind
+
+Requires Node.js 20 or later. `npm start` serves the homepage and newsletter API
+on port 11222 (override with `PORT` and optionally `HOST`). `npm run build` checks
+JavaScript syntax without starting or importing the server.
+
+Newsletter submissions are saved to `data/newsletter.jsonl` only after validation.
+Set `DATA_DIR` to a persistent, private directory in production. The directory is
+never served over HTTP. A successful signup means the address was saved; sending
+newsletters is outside this app.
+
+Every response includes an enforcing Content-Security-Policy. Scripts and styles
+must come from this server, connections and form submissions stay on this origin,
+and photos can also load from `https://images.unsplash.com`. Inline scripts,
+embedded frames, plugins, and base URL overrides are blocked. No external fonts,
+analytics, or JavaScript dependencies are used. Network, timeout, server, and
+blocked connection failures produce an accessible message on the signup form.
+
+CSP restricts resource requests; it is defense in depth and does not guarantee
+that arbitrary injected code cannot expose data (for example through navigation).
+Continue to prevent injection and serve the site over HTTPS in production.
